      "writtenOn": "2016-10-19T17:20:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting.  Everywhere else we register functors to handle particular kinds of messages, but here these messages have a subtype.  I can see an argument that we should be consistent and register a functor here as a handler, but this requires a switch statement in the functor and then a cast down to a particular type.\n\nIf we instead asked people to register an object that had different methods to receive each type of message, we would no longer need that superclass, and we move the switch statement to inside the parsing code.  The downside is that of course we register different kinds of objects for different kinds of messages.\n\nI\u0027d prefer to avoid the cast, but I can see this both ways.  What do you think?",
      "revId": "9ba19a7b73fc8e21fb7ce529e8c459487943d41f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
